<div class="su-g-accordion-faqs aem-GridColumn aem-GridColumn--default--12">













<div class="ab-g-list-exp section">
	<ul class="su12-accordion-faqs  " role="list">
		
			
			
			<li class="su12-accordion-faqs__item on" an-tr="su12_accordion faqs-vd marketing page-cta-content_click" an-ca="content click" an-ac="feature" an-la="faq:accordion:what does oled tv mean" role="listitem">
				<h3>
					<a href="javascript:void(0)" class="su12-accordion-faqs__title" aria-expanded="true" role="button">
						
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__title-text">What Does OLED TV Mean?</div>
						<span class="icon-wrap">
							<svg class="icon plus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#plus-bold" href="#plus-bold"></use></svg>
							<svg class="icon minus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#minus-bold" href="#minus-bold"></use></svg>
						</span>
					</a>
				</h3>
				<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents" id="anchor-id057">
					<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-description">An OLED TV is a type of display that uses self-lighting pixels to create its image. Unlike traditional TVs that rely on a backlight, OLED panels use organic compounds that emit light when electricity is applied — hence the name OLED, which stands for Organic Light-Emitting Diode.
Each pixel in an OLED screen can be turned on and off, or have its brightness independently adjusted. This allows for incredibly precise control over contrast and color, resulting in deep, true blacks, vibrant visuals and ultra-responsive performance. Whether you're watching movies, gaming or streaming your favorite shows, OLED technology delivers a viewing experience that's hard to match.</div>
					
					
						
					<!--
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer-wrap">
							<p class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer">...omitted...</p>
						</div>-->
						
					

					
				</div>
			</li>
		
			
			
			<li class="su12-accordion-faqs__item " an-tr="su12_accordion faqs-vd marketing page-cta-content_click" an-ca="content click" an-ac="feature" an-la="faq:accordion:dose oled have deep blacks and infinite contrast" role="listitem">
				<h3>
					<a href="javascript:void(0)" class="su12-accordion-faqs__title" aria-expanded="false" role="button">
						
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__title-text">Dose OLED have Deep blacks and infinite contrast?</div>
						<span class="icon-wrap">
							<svg class="icon plus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#plus-bold" href="#plus-bold"></use></svg>
							<svg class="icon minus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#minus-bold" href="#minus-bold"></use></svg>
						</span>
					</a>
				</h3>
				<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents" id="anchor-id147">
					<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-description">Yes, One of the most notable qualities of OLED TVs is their ability to produce truly deep blacks. Since each pixel can turn off completely, there's no light bleed from a backlight — unlike on traditional LED TVs. This results in infinite contrast, where bright elements pop against pitch-black backgrounds, creating a more immersive and cinematic viewing experience, especially in dark rooms.<br />
Samsung OLED TVs take this a step further with Glare Free (S95F), an advanced anti-glare technology that ensures these deep blacks aren’t washed out by external reflections. This keeps dark scenes rich and precise, maintaining clarity without unwanted glare.
</div>
					
					
						
					<!--
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer-wrap">
							<p class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer">...omitted...</p>
						</div>-->
						
					

					
				</div>
			</li>
		
			
			
			<li class="su12-accordion-faqs__item " an-tr="su12_accordion faqs-vd marketing page-cta-content_click" an-ca="content click" an-ac="feature" an-la="faq:accordion:dose oled vivid, lifelike colors" role="listitem">
				<h3>
					<a href="javascript:void(0)" class="su12-accordion-faqs__title" aria-expanded="false" role="button">
						
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__title-text">Dose OLED vivid, lifelike colors?</div>
						<span class="icon-wrap">
							<svg class="icon plus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#plus-bold" href="#plus-bold"></use></svg>
							<svg class="icon minus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#minus-bold" href="#minus-bold"></use></svg>
						</span>
					</a>
				</h3>
				<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents" id="anchor-id20">
					<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-description">Another area where OLED TVs truly shine is in their ability to produce rich, accurate colors. This is because their self-emissive technology lets them fine-tune color output with remarkable precision. Colors stay vivid and well-defined — even in the darkest scenes — while pixel-level light control ensures sharp detail, especially with HDR content.<br />
On Samsung OLED TVs, the true blacks, infinite contrast, HDR support and uniform color distribution all work together to deliver colors that feel almost real. Additionally, with Pantone Validated, Samsung OLED TVs ensure colors are displayed with unmatched accuracy, matching the hues intended by creators. The result is a deeply immersive viewing experience that brings every frame to life.</div>
					
					
						
					<!--
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer-wrap">
							<p class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer">...omitted...</p>
						</div>-->
						
					

					
				</div>
			</li>
		
			
			
			<li class="su12-accordion-faqs__item " an-tr="su12_accordion faqs-vd marketing page-cta-content_click" an-ca="content click" an-ac="feature" an-la="faq:accordion:are oled tvs worth it" role="listitem">
				<h3>
					<a href="javascript:void(0)" class="su12-accordion-faqs__title" aria-expanded="false" role="button">
						
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__title-text">Are OLED TVs Worth It?</div>
						<span class="icon-wrap">
							<svg class="icon plus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#plus-bold" href="#plus-bold"></use></svg>
							<svg class="icon minus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#minus-bold" href="#minus-bold"></use></svg>
						</span>
					</a>
				</h3>
				<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents" id="anchor-id383">
					<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-description">Whether OLED TVs are worth it depends on your priorities and budget. Here are some factors to consider:<br />

<br />• Deep blacks and infinite contrast : Samsung OLED TVs deliver infinite contrast with true deep blacks, enhanced by Glare Free(S95F) anti-reflection tech and OLED HDR Pro/HDR+/HDR for balanced brightness and vivid visuals in any lighting. These features create a refined, immersive experience ideal for movies, dramas, and shadow-rich content.<br />

<br />•︎ Stunning Brightness: Samsung OLED TVs achieve high peak brightness for enhanced visibility in bright spaces and improved HDR performance, while self-emissive pixels ensure precise brightness control for deeper blacks and vibrant highlights. With OLED HDR Pro, the S95F delivers lifelike visuals with unmatched contrast and detail.<br />

<br />• ︎Vivid, lifelike colors : Samsung OLED TVs excel in producing rich, accurate colors through self-emissive technology, offering vivid hues and sharp details even in dark scenes. With Pantone Validated precision, they deliver lifelike visuals, ensuring creators’ intended colors are perfectly reproduced for an immersive experience.<br />

<br />•︎ Fast response times for smooth gaming : Samsung OLED TVs feature fast response times, high refresh rates (up to 165Hz), and gaming-specific technologies like Motion Xcelerator, ALLM, and AI Game Mode for smooth, lag-free gameplay. With G-Sync Compatible and FreeSync Premium Pro, they deliver tear-free, stutter-free visuals, making them ideal for immersive gaming.<br />

<br />•︎ Elegant, ultra-thin design : Without a bulky backlight, Samsung OLED TVs like the S95F feature ultra-thin designs, minimal bezels, and a matte finish for reduced glare, blending seamlessly into modern interiors as both a functional device and a stylish statement piece.</div>
					
					
						
					<!--
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer-wrap">
							<p class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer">...omitted...</p>
						</div>-->
						
					

					
				</div>
			</li>
		
			
			
			<li class="su12-accordion-faqs__item " an-tr="su12_accordion faqs-vd marketing page-cta-content_click" an-ca="content click" an-ac="feature" an-la="faq:accordion:dose oled have fast response times for smooth gaming" role="listitem">
				<h3>
					<a href="javascript:void(0)" class="su12-accordion-faqs__title" aria-expanded="false" role="button">
						
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__title-text">Dose OLED have fast response times for smooth gaming?</div>
						<span class="icon-wrap">
							<svg class="icon plus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#plus-bold" href="#plus-bold"></use></svg>
							<svg class="icon minus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#minus-bold" href="#minus-bold"></use></svg>
						</span>
					</a>
				</h3>
				<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents" id="anchor-id497">
					<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-description">OLED TVs' self-emissive technology enables fast response times and high refresh rates, typically ranging from 120Hz to 144Hz, and even reaching up to 165Hz on certain models. This capability is attributed to the rapid pixel control method of OLED, which can turn pixels on and off extremely quickly, as well as the thin physical structure of the OLED panel itself.<br />

<br />As a result, motion remains sharp and fluid, even during fast-paced scenes, delivering a responsive and visually seamless experience with minimal blur or lag.<br />

<br />On Samsung OLED TVs, features like Motion Xcelerator, Auto Low Latency Mode (ALLM) and AI Game Mode are specifically designed to enhance motion clarity and gaming performance. Additionally, support for G-Sync Compatible (S95F) and FreeSync Premium Pro (S90F) ensures smooth, tear-free gameplay by synchronizing the TV's refresh rate with the graphics card. These technologies work together to eliminate stuttering and screen tearing, making Samsung OLED TVs an ideal choice for gamers seeking an immersive and lag-free experience.</div>
					
					
						
					<!--
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer-wrap">
							<p class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer">...omitted...</p>
						</div>-->
						
					

					
				</div>
			</li>
		
			
			
			<li class="su12-accordion-faqs__item " an-tr="su12_accordion faqs-vd marketing page-cta-content_click" an-ca="content click" an-ac="feature" an-la="faq:accordion:dose oled have elegant ultra thin design" role="listitem">
				<h3>
					<a href="javascript:void(0)" class="su12-accordion-faqs__title" aria-expanded="false" role="button">
						
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__title-text">Dose OLED have Elegant, ultra-thin design?</div>
						<span class="icon-wrap">
							<svg class="icon plus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#plus-bold" href="#plus-bold"></use></svg>
							<svg class="icon minus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#minus-bold" href="#minus-bold"></use></svg>
						</span>
					</a>
				</h3>
				<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents" id="anchor-id599">
					<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-description">Since OLED panels don’t require a bulky backlight, they can be made incredibly thin — resulting in TVs with a sleek, minimalist profile that looks stunning from every angle. Their clean lines and slim form factor blend seamlessly into modern interiors, adding a touch of sophistication to your space.<br />

<br />For example, the Samsung OLED S95F — with its ultra-thin Infinity One design, minimal bezels and a smooth matte finish that reduces glare — is designed to go beyond functionality and serve as a true statement piece. Whether mounted on the wall or placed on a stand, this TV effortlessly captivates and elevates your home’s aesthetic.</div>
					
					
						
					<!--
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer-wrap">
							<p class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer">...omitted...</p>
						</div>-->
						
					

					
				</div>
			</li>
		
			
			
			<li class="su12-accordion-faqs__item " an-tr="su12_accordion faqs-vd marketing page-cta-content_click" an-ca="content click" an-ac="feature" an-la="faq:accordion:what is the difference between oled and qled" role="listitem">
				<h3>
					<a href="javascript:void(0)" class="su12-accordion-faqs__title" aria-expanded="false" role="button">
						
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__title-text">What is the difference between OLED and QLED?</div>
						<span class="icon-wrap">
							<svg class="icon plus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#plus-bold" href="#plus-bold"></use></svg>
							<svg class="icon minus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#minus-bold" href="#minus-bold"></use></svg>
						</span>
					</a>
				</h3>
				<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents" id="anchor-id683">
					<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-description">The primary differences between OLED and QLED TVs lie in their display technologies, picture quality, and design.<br /> 

<br />• OLED (Organic Light Emitting Diode):
<br />Uses self-emissive pixels that produce their own light.
<br />Each pixel can turn off completely, enabling deep blacks and infinite contrast.<br />

<br />•QLED (Quantum Dot Light Emitting Diode):
<br />Uses a backlight combined with quantum dot technology to enhance color and brightness.</div>
					
					
						
					<!--
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer-wrap">
							<p class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer">...omitted...</p>
						</div>-->
						
					

					
				</div>
			</li>
		
			
			
			<li class="su12-accordion-faqs__item " an-tr="su12_accordion faqs-vd marketing page-cta-content_click" an-ca="content click" an-ac="feature" an-la="faq:accordion:what is the difference between oled and neo qled" role="listitem">
				<h3>
					<a href="javascript:void(0)" class="su12-accordion-faqs__title" aria-expanded="false" role="button">
						
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__title-text">What is the difference between OLED and Neo QLED? </div>
						<span class="icon-wrap">
							<svg class="icon plus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#plus-bold" href="#plus-bold"></use></svg>
							<svg class="icon minus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#minus-bold" href="#minus-bold"></use></svg>
						</span>
					</a>
				</h3>
				<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents" id="anchor-id727">
					<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-description">The main differences between OLED and Neo QLED TVs lie in their display technologies, picture quality, and specific features. Here’s a detailed comparison:<br />

<br />Key Features
<br />• OLED:
<br />Deep blacks and infinite contrast.
<br />Slim, elegant design. Fast response times for gaming.<br />

<br />• Neo QLED:
<br />Uses a backlight composed of tiny mini-LEDs combined with quantum dot technology.
<br />The mini-LEDs allow for finer control of brightness and contrast through local dimming zones.<br />

<br />Which Should You Choose?
<br />Choose OLED if you prioritize deep blacks, contrast, and a sleek design, especially for dark room viewing or cinematic experiences.
<br />Choose Neo QLED if you prefer brighter screens, improved contrast over traditional LED TVs, and affordability, particularly for well-lit rooms or larger sizes.</div>
					
					
						
					<!--
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer-wrap">
							<p class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer">...omitted...</p>
						</div>-->
						
					

					
				</div>
			</li>
		
			
			
			<li class="su12-accordion-faqs__item " an-tr="su12_accordion faqs-vd marketing page-cta-content_click" an-ca="content click" an-ac="feature" an-la="faq:accordion:what is the largest oled tv" role="listitem">
				<h3>
					<a href="javascript:void(0)" class="su12-accordion-faqs__title" aria-expanded="false" role="button">
						
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__title-text">What is the largest OLED TV?</div>
						<span class="icon-wrap">
							<svg class="icon plus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#plus-bold" href="#plus-bold"></use></svg>
							<svg class="icon minus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#minus-bold" href="#minus-bold"></use></svg>
						</span>
					</a>
				</h3>
				<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents" id="anchor-id896">
					<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-description">Samsung’s OLED TV lineup includes 2.09 m models, which are part of their premium offerings. If you’re looking for specific details about the 2.09 m model, such as pricing or availability, please check Samsung’s official website or visit a retailer for the most accurate and up-to-date information.</div>
					
					
						
					<!--
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer-wrap">
							<p class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer">...omitted...</p>
						</div>-->
						
					

					
				</div>
			</li>
		
			
			
			<li class="su12-accordion-faqs__item " an-tr="su12_accordion faqs-vd marketing page-cta-content_click" an-ca="content click" an-ac="feature" an-la="faq:accordion:is oled worth it for console gaming" role="listitem">
				<h3>
					<a href="javascript:void(0)" class="su12-accordion-faqs__title" aria-expanded="false" role="button">
						
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__title-text">Is OLED worth it for console gaming?</div>
						<span class="icon-wrap">
							<svg class="icon plus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#plus-bold" href="#plus-bold"></use></svg>
							<svg class="icon minus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#minus-bold" href="#minus-bold"></use></svg>
						</span>
					</a>
				</h3>
				<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents" id="anchor-id938">
					<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-description">Yes, a Samsung OLED TV is an excellent choice for console gaming, especially if you value premium picture quality and advanced gaming features.<br />

<br />Here’s why Samsung OLED is worth considering for gaming.
<br />1. Low Input Lag and Fast Response Time: Samsung OLED TVs are optimized for gaming with ultra-low input lag and fast response times, ensuring smooth and responsive gameplay.
<br />2. Advanced Gaming Features: Samsung OLED TVs support HDMI 2.1, which enables features like 4K at 120 Hz (or higher) for ultra-smooth motion, Variable Refresh Rate (VRR) to eliminate screen tearing, Auto Low Latency Mode (ALLM) to automatically switch to gaming mode, and Nvidia G-Sync and FreeSync Premium Pro for enhanced compatibility with gaming consoles and PCs.
<br />3. Stunning Visuals: Samsung OLED TVs are well-suited for immersive single-player games with deep blacks, vibrant colors and sharp details, thanks to Samsung OLED technology.
<br />4. Wide Viewing Angles: Colors and contrast remain consistent even at extreme angles, making these TVs ideal for multiplayer setups or group gaming sessions.
<br />5. Size Options: Samsung OLED TVs are available in a variety of sizes ranging from 55 inches to 83 inches. Smaller sizes (e.g. 55 inches) are ideal for compact spaces, while larger sizes (e.g. 83 inches) suit dedicated home theaters.<br /></div>
					
					
						
					<!--
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer-wrap">
							<p class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer">...omitted...</p>
						</div>-->
						
					

					
				</div>
			</li>
		
			
			
			<li class="su12-accordion-faqs__item " an-tr="su12_accordion faqs-vd marketing page-cta-content_click" an-ca="content click" an-ac="feature" an-la="faq:accordion:does oled have good viewing angles" role="listitem">
				<h3>
					<a href="javascript:void(0)" class="su12-accordion-faqs__title" aria-expanded="false" role="button">
						
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__title-text">Does OLED have good viewing angles?</div>
						<span class="icon-wrap">
							<svg class="icon plus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#plus-bold" href="#plus-bold"></use></svg>
							<svg class="icon minus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#minus-bold" href="#minus-bold"></use></svg>
						</span>
					</a>
				</h3>
				<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents" id="anchor-id103">
					<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-description">Yes, OLED TVs have excellent viewing angles. This can be explained by the following reasons:
<br />- Self-Emissive Pixels: OLED TVs use organic light-emitting diodes that emit their own light. Since each pixel produces its own light independently, the image quality remains consistent regardless of the viewing angle.
<br />- Color Accuracy and Contrast: OLED TVs maintain accurate colors and deep blacks even at extreme angles.
<br />- Wide Viewing Angle Technology: Modern OLED TVs incorporate advanced panel designs that enhance viewing angles further, ensuring minimal distortion or color washout.<br />

<br />There are several benefits of having wide viewing angles in Samsung OLED TVs:
<br />- Ideal for Multiplayer Gaming: Gamers can comfortably play with friends sitting at different angles without losing image quality.
<br />- Great for Large Rooms: In larger living spaces or home theaters, viewers seated off-center can still enjoy the same vibrant and immersive picture.
<br />- Perfect for Group Watching: Whether it’s a movie night or sports event, everyone in the room gets a clear and consistent view of the screen.<br />

<br />In conclusion, OLED TVs offer exceptional viewing angles, making them an excellent choice for multi-viewer setups, large rooms, or anyone who values consistent picture quality from any position in the room.</div>
					
					
						
					<!--
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer-wrap">
							<p class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer">...omitted...</p>
						</div>-->
						
					

					
				</div>
			</li>
		
			
			
			<li class="su12-accordion-faqs__item " an-tr="su12_accordion faqs-vd marketing page-cta-content_click" an-ca="content click" an-ac="feature" an-la="faq:accordion:are oled tvs flicker free" role="listitem">
				<h3>
					<a href="javascript:void(0)" class="su12-accordion-faqs__title" aria-expanded="false" role="button">
						
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__title-text">Are OLED TVs flicker-free?</div>
						<span class="icon-wrap">
							<svg class="icon plus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#plus-bold" href="#plus-bold"></use></svg>
							<svg class="icon minus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#minus-bold" href="#minus-bold"></use></svg>
						</span>
					</a>
				</h3>
				<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents" id="anchor-id1154">
					<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-description">Yes, OLED TVs are generally considered flicker-free thanks to their pixel-level lighting technology.<br />

<br />This is because these displays use organic light-emitting diodes that emit light individually when electricity is applied. Each OLED pixel can turn on and off completely, eliminating the need for flickering to control brightness. Instead, on an OLED TV brightness is smoothly controlled through analog dimming, which varies voltage rather than rapidly cycling light.<br />

<br />Benefits of having flicker-free OLED TVs include:
<br />- Reduced Eye Strain: Flicker-free displays are easier on the eyes, especially during prolonged viewing sessions.
<br />- Better Visual Comfort: Ideal for gamers, movie enthusiasts, or anyone who spends extended periods in front of the TV.
<br />- Consistent Picture Quality: No flickering ensures a stable and natural image, enhancing the overall viewing experience.<br />

<br />Samsung OLED TVs are flicker-free, making them a great choice for viewers who prioritize eye comfort and a smooth viewing experience. If you’re sensitive to flickering or plan to use your TV for extended periods, these displays are an excellent option.</div>
					
					
						
					<!--
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer-wrap">
							<p class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer">...omitted...</p>
						</div>-->
						
					

					
				</div>
			</li>
		
			
			
			<li class="su12-accordion-faqs__item " an-tr="su12_accordion faqs-vd marketing page-cta-content_click" an-ca="content click" an-ac="feature" an-la="faq:accordion:how to reduce glare on samsung oled tvs" role="listitem">
				<h3>
					<a href="javascript:void(0)" class="su12-accordion-faqs__title" aria-expanded="false" role="button">
						
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__title-text">How to reduce glare on Samsung OLED TVs?</div>
						<span class="icon-wrap">
							<svg class="icon plus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#plus-bold" href="#plus-bold"></use></svg>
							<svg class="icon minus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#minus-bold" href="#minus-bold"></use></svg>
						</span>
					</a>
				</h3>
				<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents" id="anchor-id129">
					<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-description">Glare occurs when light from windows, lamps, or other sources reflects off the TV screen, making it difficult to see the image clearly.<br />

<br />While they offer stunning picture quality, OLED TVs can be more prone to glare due to their glossy screens.<br />

<br />However, on Samsung OLED TVs, Glare Free, our proprietary anti-glare technology ensures that the image remains clear from distracting reflections.</div>
					
					
						
					<!--
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer-wrap">
							<p class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer">...omitted...</p>
						</div>-->
						
					

					
				</div>
			</li>
		
			
			
			<li class="su12-accordion-faqs__item " an-tr="su12_accordion faqs-vd marketing page-cta-content_click" an-ca="content click" an-ac="feature" an-la="faq:accordion: how long do oled tvs last" role="listitem">
				<h3>
					<a href="javascript:void(0)" class="su12-accordion-faqs__title" aria-expanded="false" role="button">
						
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__title-text"> How long do OLED TVs last?</div>
						<span class="icon-wrap">
							<svg class="icon plus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#plus-bold" href="#plus-bold"></use></svg>
							<svg class="icon minus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#minus-bold" href="#minus-bold"></use></svg>
						</span>
					</a>
				</h3>
				<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents" id="anchor-id1389">
					<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-description">OLED TVs typically have a lifespan of around 50,000 to 100,000 hours of use. This translates to approximately 10 to 20 years of normal viewing. However, the actual lifespan can vary depending on factors such as:<br />

<br />•  Usage intensity: Frequent or prolonged use may shorten the lifespan.
<br />•  Brightness settings: Higher brightness levels can accelerate screen aging.
<br />•  Content type: Static images or logos can cause burn-in over time.
<br />•  Manufacturing quality: Different brands and models may have varying durability.<br />

<br />To maximize the lifespan of an OLED TV, it’s recommended to avoid displaying static images for extended periods, adjust brightness settings appropriately, and follow the manufacturer’s maintenance guidelines.</div>
					
					
						
					<!--
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer-wrap">
							<p class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer">...omitted...</p>
						</div>-->
						
					

					
				</div>
			</li>
		
			
			
			<li class="su12-accordion-faqs__item " an-tr="su12_accordion faqs-vd marketing page-cta-content_click" an-ca="content click" an-ac="feature" an-la="faq:accordion:which samsung oled tv should i buy" role="listitem">
				<h3>
					<a href="javascript:void(0)" class="su12-accordion-faqs__title" aria-expanded="false" role="button">
						
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__title-text">Which Samsung OLED TV should I buy?</div>
						<span class="icon-wrap">
							<svg class="icon plus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#plus-bold" href="#plus-bold"></use></svg>
							<svg class="icon minus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#minus-bold" href="#minus-bold"></use></svg>
						</span>
					</a>
				</h3>
				<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents" id="anchor-id1496">
					<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-description">As we've seen above, Samsung OLED TVs are some of the best among OLED TVs, as they come equipped with various advanced technologies that make OLED TVs even more excellent.<br />

<br />But which Samsung OLED TV model you should choose in particular depends on your specific needs and preferences.</div>
					
					
						
					<!--
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer-wrap">
							<p class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer">...omitted...</p>
						</div>-->
						
					

					
				</div>
			</li>
		
			
			
			<li class="su12-accordion-faqs__item " an-tr="su12_accordion faqs-vd marketing page-cta-content_click" an-ca="content click" an-ac="feature" an-la="faq:accordion:why samsung oled tvs are an outstanding choice" role="listitem">
				<h3>
					<a href="javascript:void(0)" class="su12-accordion-faqs__title" aria-expanded="false" role="button">
						
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__title-text">Why Samsung OLED TVs Are an Outstanding Choice</div>
						<span class="icon-wrap">
							<svg class="icon plus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#plus-bold" href="#plus-bold"></use></svg>
							<svg class="icon minus" focusable="false"><use xlink:href="#minus-bold" href="#minus-bold"></use></svg>
						</span>
					</a>
				</h3>
				<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents" id="anchor-id1548">
					<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-description">As we’ve seen, OLED TVs — in particular ones designed by Samsung — stand out as a worthwhile investment for anyone seeking exceptional visual quality, innovative features, and sleek design. With their vibrant picture performance, advanced gaming capabilities, and smart energy-saving options like AI Energy Mode, they cater to a wide range of lifestyles and preferences. Whether you're passionate about movies, gaming, or modern aesthetics, Samsung OLED TVs offer a premium experience that truly justifies their value.</div>
					
					
						
					<!--
						<div class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer-wrap">
							<p class="su12-accordion-faqs__contents-disclaimer">...omitted...</p>
						</div>-->
						
					

					
				</div>
			</li>
		
	</ul>
</div>

  <script type="application/ld+json" data-type="seo" data-object-type="FAQPage" data-id="a401d7cb-1052-454f-b53d-33f55216e7e3">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","@id":"https://www.samsung.com/pk/tvs/oled-tv/highlights/#FAQ","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What Does OLED TV Mean?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"An OLED TV is a type of display that uses self-lighting pixels to create its image. Unlike traditional TVs that rely on a backlight, OLED panels use organic compounds that emit light when electricity is applied — hence the name OLED, which stands for Organic Light-Emitting Diode.\r\nEach pixel in an OLED screen can be turned on and off, or have its brightness independently adjusted. This allows for incredibly precise control over contrast and color, resulting in deep, true blacks, vibrant visuals and ultra-responsive performance. Whether you're watching movies, gaming or streaming your favorite shows, OLED technology delivers a viewing experience that's hard to match."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Dose OLED have Deep blacks and infinite contrast?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, One of the most notable qualities of OLED TVs is their ability to produce truly deep blacks. Since each pixel can turn off completely, there's no light bleed from a backlight — unlike on traditional LED TVs. This results in infinite contrast, where bright elements pop against pitch-black backgrounds, creating a more immersive and cinematic viewing experience, especially in dark rooms.<br>\r\nSamsung OLED TVs take this a step further with Glare Free (S95F), an advanced anti-glare technology that ensures these deep blacks aren’t washed out by external reflections. This keeps dark scenes rich and precise, maintaining clarity without unwanted glare.\r\n"}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Dose OLED vivid, lifelike colors?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Another area where OLED TVs truly shine is in their ability to produce rich, accurate colors. This is because their self-emissive technology lets them fine-tune color output with remarkable precision. Colors stay vivid and well-defined — even in the darkest scenes — while pixel-level light control ensures sharp detail, especially with HDR content.<br>\r\nOn Samsung OLED TVs, the true blacks, infinite contrast, HDR support and uniform color distribution all work together to deliver colors that feel almost real. Additionally, with Pantone Validated, Samsung OLED TVs ensure colors are displayed with unmatched accuracy, matching the hues intended by creators. The result is a deeply immersive viewing experience that brings every frame to life."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Are OLED TVs Worth It?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Whether OLED TVs are worth it depends on your priorities and budget. Here are some factors to consider:<br>\r\n\r\n<br>• Deep blacks and infinite contrast : Samsung OLED TVs deliver infinite contrast with true deep blacks, enhanced by Glare Free(S95F) anti-reflection tech and OLED HDR Pro/HDR+/HDR for balanced brightness and vivid visuals in any lighting. These features create a refined, immersive experience ideal for movies, dramas, and shadow-rich content.<br>\r\n\r\n<br>•︎ Stunning Brightness: Samsung OLED TVs achieve high peak brightness for enhanced visibility in bright spaces and improved HDR performance, while self-emissive pixels ensure precise brightness control for deeper blacks and vibrant highlights. With OLED HDR Pro, the S95F delivers lifelike visuals with unmatched contrast and detail.<br>\r\n\r\n<br>• ︎Vivid, lifelike colors : Samsung OLED TVs excel in producing rich, accurate colors through self-emissive technology, offering vivid hues and sharp details even in dark scenes. With Pantone Validated precision, they deliver lifelike visuals, ensuring creators’ intended colors are perfectly reproduced for an immersive experience.<br>\r\n\r\n<br>•︎ Fast response times for smooth gaming : Samsung OLED TVs feature fast response times, high refresh rates (up to 165Hz), and gaming-specific technologies like Motion Xcelerator, ALLM, and AI Game Mode for smooth, lag-free gameplay. With G-Sync Compatible and FreeSync Premium Pro, they deliver tear-free, stutter-free visuals, making them ideal for immersive gaming.<br>\r\n\r\n<br>•︎ Elegant, ultra-thin design : Without a bulky backlight, Samsung OLED TVs like the S95F feature ultra-thin designs, minimal bezels, and a matte finish for reduced glare, blending seamlessly into modern interiors as both a functional device and a stylish statement piece."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Dose OLED have fast response times for smooth gaming?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"OLED TVs' self-emissive technology enables fast response times and high refresh rates, typically ranging from 120Hz to 144Hz, and even reaching up to 165Hz on certain models. This capability is attributed to the rapid pixel control method of OLED, which can turn pixels on and off extremely quickly, as well as the thin physical structure of the OLED panel itself.<br>\r\n\r\n<br>As a result, motion remains sharp and fluid, even during fast-paced scenes, delivering a responsive and visually seamless experience with minimal blur or lag.<br>\r\n\r\n<br>On Samsung OLED TVs, features like Motion Xcelerator, Auto Low Latency Mode (ALLM) and AI Game Mode are specifically designed to enhance motion clarity and gaming performance. Additionally, support for G-Sync Compatible (S95F) and FreeSync Premium Pro (S90F) ensures smooth, tear-free gameplay by synchronizing the TV's refresh rate with the graphics card. These technologies work together to eliminate stuttering and screen tearing, making Samsung OLED TVs an ideal choice for gamers seeking an immersive and lag-free experience."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Dose OLED have Elegant, ultra-thin design?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Since OLED panels don’t require a bulky backlight, they can be made incredibly thin — resulting in TVs with a sleek, minimalist profile that looks stunning from every angle. Their clean lines and slim form factor blend seamlessly into modern interiors, adding a touch of sophistication to your space.<br>\r\n\r\n<br>For example, the Samsung OLED S95F — with its ultra-thin Infinity One design, minimal bezels and a smooth matte finish that reduces glare — is designed to go beyond functionality and serve as a true statement piece. Whether mounted on the wall or placed on a stand, this TV effortlessly captivates and elevates your home’s aesthetic."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the difference between OLED and QLED?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The primary differences between OLED and QLED TVs lie in their display technologies, picture quality, and design.<br> \r\n\r\n<br>• OLED (Organic Light Emitting Diode):\r\n<br>Uses self-emissive pixels that produce their own light.\r\n<br>Each pixel can turn off completely, enabling deep blacks and infinite contrast.<br>\r\n\r\n<br>•QLED (Quantum Dot Light Emitting Diode):\r\n<br>Uses a backlight combined with quantum dot technology to enhance color and brightness."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the difference between OLED and Neo QLED? ","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The main differences between OLED and Neo QLED TVs lie in their display technologies, picture quality, and specific features. Here’s a detailed comparison:<br>\r\n\r\n<br>Key Features\r\n<br>• OLED:\r\n<br>Deep blacks and infinite contrast.\r\n<br>Slim, elegant design. Fast response times for gaming.<br>\r\n\r\n<br>• Neo QLED:\r\n<br>Uses a backlight composed of tiny mini-LEDs combined with quantum dot technology.\r\n<br>The mini-LEDs allow for finer control of brightness and contrast through local dimming zones.<br>\r\n\r\n<br>Which Should You Choose?\r\n<br>Choose OLED if you prioritize deep blacks, contrast, and a sleek design, especially for dark room viewing or cinematic experiences.\r\n<br>Choose Neo QLED if you prefer brighter screens, improved contrast over traditional LED TVs, and affordability, particularly for well-lit rooms or larger sizes."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the largest OLED TV?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Samsung’s OLED TV lineup includes 2.09 m models, which are part of their premium offerings. If you’re looking for specific details about the 2.09 m model, such as pricing or availability, please check Samsung’s official website or visit a retailer for the most accurate and up-to-date information."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is OLED worth it for console gaming?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, a Samsung OLED TV is an excellent choice for console gaming, especially if you value premium picture quality and advanced gaming features.<br>\r\n\r\n<br>Here’s why Samsung OLED is worth considering for gaming.\r\n<br>1. Low Input Lag and Fast Response Time: Samsung OLED TVs are optimized for gaming with ultra-low input lag and fast response times, ensuring smooth and responsive gameplay.\r\n<br>2. Advanced Gaming Features: Samsung OLED TVs support HDMI 2.1, which enables features like 4K at 120 Hz (or higher) for ultra-smooth motion, Variable Refresh Rate (VRR) to eliminate screen tearing, Auto Low Latency Mode (ALLM) to automatically switch to gaming mode, and Nvidia G-Sync and FreeSync Premium Pro for enhanced compatibility with gaming consoles and PCs.\r\n<br>3. Stunning Visuals: Samsung OLED TVs are well-suited for immersive single-player games with deep blacks, vibrant colors and sharp details, thanks to Samsung OLED technology.\r\n<br>4. Wide Viewing Angles: Colors and contrast remain consistent even at extreme angles, making these TVs ideal for multiplayer setups or group gaming sessions.\r\n<br>5. Size Options: Samsung OLED TVs are available in a variety of sizes ranging from 55 inches to 83 inches. Smaller sizes (e.g. 55 inches) are ideal for compact spaces, while larger sizes (e.g. 83 inches) suit dedicated home theaters.<br>"}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does OLED have good viewing angles?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, OLED TVs have excellent viewing angles. This can be explained by the following reasons:\r\n<br>- Self-Emissive Pixels: OLED TVs use organic light-emitting diodes that emit their own light. Since each pixel produces its own light independently, the image quality remains consistent regardless of the viewing angle.\r\n<br>- Color Accuracy and Contrast: OLED TVs maintain accurate colors and deep blacks even at extreme angles.\r\n<br>- Wide Viewing Angle Technology: Modern OLED TVs incorporate advanced panel designs that enhance viewing angles further, ensuring minimal distortion or color washout.<br>\r\n\r\n<br>There are several benefits of having wide viewing angles in Samsung OLED TVs:\r\n<br>- Ideal for Multiplayer Gaming: Gamers can comfortably play with friends sitting at different angles without losing image quality.\r\n<br>- Great for Large Rooms: In larger living spaces or home theaters, viewers seated off-center can still enjoy the same vibrant and immersive picture.\r\n<br>- Perfect for Group Watching: Whether it’s a movie night or sports event, everyone in the room gets a clear and consistent view of the screen.<br>\r\n\r\n<br>In conclusion, OLED TVs offer exceptional viewing angles, making them an excellent choice for multi-viewer setups, large rooms, or anyone who values consistent picture quality from any position in the room."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Are OLED TVs flicker-free?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, OLED TVs are generally considered flicker-free thanks to their pixel-level lighting technology.<br>\r\n\r\n<br>This is because these displays use organic light-emitting diodes that emit light individually when electricity is applied. Each OLED pixel can turn on and off completely, eliminating the need for flickering to control brightness. Instead, on an OLED TV brightness is smoothly controlled through analog dimming, which varies voltage rather than rapidly cycling light.<br>\r\n\r\n<br>Benefits of having flicker-free OLED TVs include:\r\n<br>- Reduced Eye Strain: Flicker-free displays are easier on the eyes, especially during prolonged viewing sessions.\r\n<br>- Better Visual Comfort: Ideal for gamers, movie enthusiasts, or anyone who spends extended periods in front of the TV.\r\n<br>- Consistent Picture Quality: No flickering ensures a stable and natural image, enhancing the overall viewing experience.<br>\r\n\r\n<br>Samsung OLED TVs are flicker-free, making them a great choice for viewers who prioritize eye comfort and a smooth viewing experience. If you’re sensitive to flickering or plan to use your TV for extended periods, these displays are an excellent option."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How to reduce glare on Samsung OLED TVs?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Glare occurs when light from windows, lamps, or other sources reflects off the TV screen, making it difficult to see the image clearly.<br>\r\n\r\n<br>While they offer stunning picture quality, OLED TVs can be more prone to glare due to their glossy screens.<br>\r\n\r\n<br>However, on Samsung OLED TVs, Glare Free, our proprietary anti-glare technology ensures that the image remains clear from distracting reflections."}},{"@type":"Question","name":" How long do OLED TVs last?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"OLED TVs typically have a lifespan of around 50,000 to 100,000 hours of use. This translates to approximately 10 to 20 years of normal viewing. However, the actual lifespan can vary depending on factors such as:<br>\r\n\r\n<br>•  Usage intensity: Frequent or prolonged use may shorten the lifespan.\r\n<br>•  Brightness settings: Higher brightness levels can accelerate screen aging.\r\n<br>•  Content type: Static images or logos can cause burn-in over time.\r\n<br>•  Manufacturing quality: Different brands and models may have varying durability.<br>\r\n\r\n<br>To maximize the lifespan of an OLED TV, it’s recommended to avoid displaying static images for extended periods, adjust brightness settings appropriately, and follow the manufacturer’s maintenance guidelines."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Which Samsung OLED TV should I buy?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"As we've seen above, Samsung OLED TVs are some of the best among OLED TVs, as they come equipped with various advanced technologies that make OLED TVs even more excellent.<br>\r\n\r\n<br>But which Samsung OLED TV model you should choose in particular depends on your specific needs and preferences."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Why Samsung OLED TVs Are an Outstanding Choice","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"As we’ve seen, OLED TVs — in particular ones designed by Samsung — stand out as a worthwhile investment for anyone seeking exceptional visual quality, innovative features, and sleek design. With their vibrant picture performance, advanced gaming capabilities, and smart energy-saving options like AI Energy Mode, they cater to a wide range of lifestyles and preferences. Whether you're passionate about movies, gaming, or modern aesthetics, Samsung OLED TVs offer a premium experience that truly justifies their value."}}]}</script>


</div>
